# Quality-eval (PRD 2) builds the TS/Go fixtures too; their generated index
# state (.neuralmind/, index_ir.json) is not source. graphify-out/ for those
# fixtures IS committed, so only ignore .neuralmind here.
tests/fixtures/sample_project_ts/.neuralmind/
tests/fixtures/sample_project_go/.neuralmind/
tests/benchmark/quality.md
/graphify-out/

# Per-project state (generated, not source). CLAUDE.md: "Generated state
# lives in <project>/.neuralmind/ — never committed." Four files
# (index_ir.json, ir_meta.json, audit_events.jsonl, update.log) had been
# force-added and shipped on public main; untracked as of this commit.
.neuralmind/

# Internal commercial + go-to-market material. This repo is PUBLIC.
# These were live on main and are business-confidential: the financial
# model carries 5-year revenue/cost projections, blended ARPU and an
# annual price escalator — i.e. a customer could read our margins before
# negotiating, and LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md §6 itself declares "Licensor's
# pricing and product roadmap are Licensor's confidential information."
# Keep these local; do not commit.
#
# NOTE: LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md (terms + price list) is deliberately NOT
# ignored — published terms are an asset for an open-core project. It is
# the reasoning *behind* the prices that stays private.
/CFO_ADVISORY_DECK.pptx
/LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.docx
/PROJECT_LINKEDIN_NEURALMIND.md
/NEURALMIND_LINKEDIN_POSTS.md
/contracts/
/docs/market-research/
/docs/LINKEDIN-POST-DRAFT.md

# GitHub Actions runner log fragments occasionally land at the repo root
# matching job names (Build Package/, Lint/, Test (Python 3.x)/, Type Check/)
# with a single system.txt inside. They were committed once around v0.4.0;
# guard against recurrence.
/Build Package/
/Lint/
/Test (Python 3.10)/
/Test (Python 3.11)/
/Test (Python 3.12)/
/Type Check/

# Generated by the backend parity gate (evals/parity/run.py)
evals/parity/parity_report.json
evals/parity/parity_report.md

# Public-benchmark working clones (regenerated by evals/public/run.py)
.bench-work/
.env
.env
.env
